WEBVTT

00:01:58.272 --> 00:02:01.446
not the sound of the fans in the computer.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.779
CA: So this is astonishing,

00:02:02.803 --> 00:02:05.481
because working this way,

00:02:05.505 --> 00:02:08.493
you're able to run this vast
technology empire --

00:02:08.517 --> 00:02:09.738
it is an empire --

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:13.462
so that's an amazing testament
to the power of open source.

00:02:13.486 --> 00:02:17.662
Tell us how you got
to understand open source

00:02:17.686 --> 00:02:19.938
and how it lead
to the development of Linux.

00:02:21.546 --> 00:02:23.051
LT: I mean, I still work alone.

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:26.642
Really -- I work alone in my house,

00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:28.056
often in my bathrobe.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.641
When a photographer shows up, I dress up,